================================================================================
Third-Party Software
================================================================================

The NOVA installer bundles the following third-party software, unmodified, so
that end users do not need to separately install a compiler toolchain. NOVA
itself does not modify or fork any of the below; it distributes official
upstream release artifacts as-is.

LLVM, Clang, LLD
  https://llvm.org/
  Licensed under the Apache License v2.0 with LLVM Exceptions.
  See https://llvm.org/LICENSE.txt for the full license text.
  Used on Linux and macOS installs, and as the underlying toolchain for the
  Windows install (via llvm-mingw, below).

llvm-mingw (mingw-w64)
  https://github.com/mstorsjo/llvm-mingw
  https://www.mingw-w64.org/
  llvm-mingw packages Clang/LLD (Apache-2.0 with LLVM Exceptions, as above)
  together with the mingw-w64 runtime and headers. The mingw-w64 project
  itself aggregates contributions under a mix of permissive licenses (chiefly
  public-domain, MIT, and BSD-style terms across its constituent headers and
  runtime libraries) rather than a single unified license.
  NOTE FOR MAINTAINERS: the authoritative, complete license text is the
  COPYING.MinGW-w64-runtime file shipped inside the actual llvm-mingw release
  archive bundled with each NOVA installer build — copy it here verbatim (do
  not hand-transcribe or paraphrase it) the first time a real llvm-mingw
  archive is packaged, so this NOTICE reflects the exact bundled version.
  Used on the Windows install (see NOVA_DESIGN/decisions/windows_toolchain_abi.md
  for why NOVA's Windows target uses the mingw-w64 ABI by default).
